msgid "See this Block with the NEW operator (green oval):"
msgstr "このブロックを新しいオペレーター（緑の楕円）でご覧ください。"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:177
msgid "PanTiltHolder"
msgstr "PanTiltHolder"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:177
msgid "Examples of Pan/Tilt Blocks"
msgstr "パン/チルトブロックの例"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:179
msgid ""
"It’s **not needed** if the OpMode will call ``getPanTilt()`` and assign it "
"to the variable, as shown above (yellow arrow)."
msgstr ""
"Op Modeが ``getPanTilt()`` を呼び出し、それを変数に割り当てる場合、上記のように（黄色の矢印） **not needed** "
"になります。"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:182
msgid ""
"It **is needed** if instead the OpMode will next try to get (or set) that "
"variable’s pan and/or tilt values, or try to pass that variable to "
"``setPanTiltHolder()``. The values will be zero."
msgstr ""
"次に、Op Modeはその変数のパンおよび/またはチルト値を取得（または設定）しようとするか、またはその変数を "
"``setPanTiltHolder()`` に渡そうとします。その値はゼロになります。"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:187
msgid "Gain and Exposure Test OpMode"
msgstr "ゲインと露出テスト Op Mode"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:189
msgid ""
"The SDK offers a built-in test OpMode to optimize Gain and Exposure. See the"
" Sample Java Sample called ``ConceptAprilTagOptimizeExposure.java``."
msgstr ""
"SDKは、ゲインと露出を最適化するための組み込みテストOp Modeを提供します。 ``__RST_FILEPATH_0__`` "
"というサンプルJavaサンプルを参照してください。"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:193
msgid "From its introduction notes:"
msgstr "導入ノートから:"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:195
msgid ""
"*This OpMode determines the best Exposure for minimizing image motion-blur "
"on a webcam. Note that it is not possible to control the exposure for a "
"Phone Camera, so if you are using a Phone for the Robot Controller this "
"OpMode/Feature only applies to an externally connected Webcam.*"
msgstr ""
"*This OpMode determines the best Exposure for minimizing image motion-blur "
"on a webcam. Note that it is not possible to control the exposure for a "
"Phone Camera, so if you are using a Phone for the Robot Controller this "
"OpMode/Feature only applies to an externally connected Webcam.*"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:201
msgid ""
"*The goal is to determine the smallest (shortest) Exposure value that still "
"provides reliable Tag Detection. Starting with the minimum Exposure and "
"maximum Gain, the exposure is slowly increased until the Tag is detected "
"reliably from the likely operational distance.*"
msgstr ""
"*The goal is to determine the smallest (shortest) Exposure value that still "
"provides reliable Tag Detection. Starting with the minimum Exposure and "
"maximum Gain, the exposure is slowly increased until the Tag is detected "
"reliably from the likely operational distance.*"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:206
msgid ""
"*The best way to run this optimization is to view the camera preview screen "
"while changing the exposure and gain.*"
msgstr ""
"*The best way to run this optimization is to view the camera preview screen "
"while changing the exposure and gain.*"

#: ../../source/apriltag/vision_portal/visionportal_camera_controls/visionportal-camera-controls.rst:209
msgid ""
"*To do this, you need to view the RobotController screen directly (not from "
"Driver Station) This can be done directly from a RC phone screen (if you are"
" using an external Webcam), but for a Control Hub you must either plug an "
"HDMI monitor into the Control Hub HDMI port, or use an external viewer "
"program like scrcpy (https://scrcpy.org/)*"
msgstr ""
"*To do this, you need to view the RobotController screen directly (not from "
"Driver Station) This can be done directly from a RC phone screen (if you are"
" using an external Webcam), but for a Control Hub you must either plug an "
"HDMI monitor into the Control Hub HDMI port, or use an external viewer "
"program like scrcpy (__RST_URL_0__)*"

